From 3cc388a8843b289132e939e3f1fce1f2b53e54b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 13:56:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 59/71] kernel: vendor ReSukiSU (KernelSU) and wire it into the
 build

ReSukiSU is the non-GKI branch of KernelSU (kernel 3.4+).  This kernel is
4.14, which has no GKI2 syscall tracepoints, so CONFIG_KSU_MANUAL_HOOK is used.

The source is vendored under KernelSU/ rather than added as a git submodule:
this tree is handed over as a tarball/zip where a submodule is lost, and git
refuses to track any path containing a ".git" component.  Only what the kernel
build consumes is kept (KernelSU/kernel + KernelSU/uapi + LICENSE), see
KernelSU/VENDORED.md for provenance and update instructions.

* drivers/kernelsu -> ../KernelSU/kernel, exactly like upstream kernel/setup.sh
* drivers/Makefile + drivers/Kconfig: build and expose the driver
* KernelSU/kernel/Kbuild: vendored-mode fixes -- no KernelSU/.git, fixed
  version values (KSU_VERSION 35144 = ReSukiSU v4.2.0-rc2, above the manager's
  MINIMAL_SUPPORTED_KERNEL of 35002) and -I$(objtree)/security/selinux for the
  generated flask.h that compat/kernel_compat.h pulls in
* build_eebbk_clang11.sh: build security/selinux and init up front, so
  drivers/kernelsu cannot race the headers they generate under -j
* configs: CONFIG_KSU=y + CONFIG_KSU_MANUAL_HOOK=y (+ KSU_DEBUG only in the
  debug config); SUSFS stays off (5.10+ GKI only), and the SELinux static
  symbol exports are unnecessary because CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL is already set
* tools/ksu: the anchored, idempotent scripts that produced all of the above

Verified on the device: Image.gz builds clean, KernelSU reports
"driver version: 35144 ... ABI: aarch64, Work mode: Built-in", and WiFi, the
hall sensors, the elevator and the audio stack are all still intact.

Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
